# Data conversion between bit and kilobyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and kilobyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0001KB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0001KB; backward, converting 1KB to 8000b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5KB yields 12000.0b.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(KB))
backward_whole: int = 1KB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0001KB
0.0001KB
8000b
12000.0b

<<< stderr
